@*
    Audit Configuration -- the Scope Builder step (545, 2026-11-13).

    REQUEST (sir): resolving the scope at configuration time is too early
    -- planning and the execution come later, by when the data has changed.
    The scope is now resolved when an execution is created
    (sp_org_assurance_execution_materialize, 545), and Scope Resolution is
    no longer a configuration step.

    What stays is the Preview: under the Scope Builder, the existing Scope
    Resolution screen ("Preview Resolve Now", the snapshots it made and
    their entities) shows what the SAVED scope matches today -- a check
    only; nothing uses these PREVIEW snapshots any more.

    Both screens are hosted unchanged. The flow shell binds both to the
    audit for this step (SCOPED 'scope' -> oaScope and oaRs,
    Partials/_audit-flow-shell).
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/org-assurance-scope-builder" model="Model" />

<div class="oa-scope-preview">
    <div class="oa-ws-section-head"><h2>Preview</h2></div>
    <p class="oa-ws-section-hint">What the saved scope matches today. Save the scope first. This is only a check: the scope is resolved again when an execution is created.</p>
    <partial name="Partials/org-assurance-scope-resolution" model="Model" />
</div>
